    <Options>
      <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
        <Vermiculite code="3">
          <English>No Vermiculite</English>
          <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
        </Vermiculite>
      </Main>
      <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="2" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:
-	Attic hatch
-	Exterior doors
-	Lights fixtures
-	Receptacles
-	Electrical panel
-	Perimeter header joist
-	Furnace
-	Basement

Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings. You can receive a $5000 rebate to increase the air sealing of your building. In order to receive the rebate, the final infiltration test should reach 1.5 air changing per hour (ACH).
</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-12. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for a $12 000 rebate for the above grade exterior walls with the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level. </mainWalls>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-40. You are eligible for a $2500 rebate for attic insulation for the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level.</ceilings>
                <foundation>Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  You are eligible to a $12000 rebate for below grade wall with the addition of a minimum of R-20 over the existing insulation level.</foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled. You can receive a $120/window for a maximum of $1800.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <AdditionalComments>ADDITIONAL COMMENTS
You can visit the Good Energy program to learn more about all offered rebate and programs by following the link below:
https://yukon.ca/en/buildings-and-homes

DEPRESSURIZATION TEST
The depressurization test performed as shown a risk of combustion gas spillage. Therefore, we recommend verifying your carbon monoxide detectors regularly.


 
</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
        <Community>N/A</Community>
      </GreenerHomes>
